  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p class=&quot;MsoNormal&quot; style=&quot;margin: 18pt -34.6pt 12pt 0cm; line-height: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;The quality of accommodation for future occupiers would be of a significantly poor standard which fails to meet minimum size standards for a three-bedroom, 2-storey development, fails to provide sufficient level of outlook, privacy or daylight into all habitable rooms, fails provide any outdoor private amenity space and the application has not submitted sufficient information to demonstrate that internal ceiling heights would meet the required standard. Therefore, the development would cause harm to the amenity of future occupiers and would not meet the standards of policy 53, 56 of Waltham Forests LP1 (2024) or policy D6 of the London Plan (2021).&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;MsoNormal&quot; style=&quot;margin: 18pt -34.6pt 12pt 0cm; line-height: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p class=&quot;MsoNormal&quot; style=&quot;margin-top:18.0pt;margin-right:-34.6pt;margin-bottom:\r\n12.0pt;margin-left:0cm;line-height:normal&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:12.0pt;\r\nfont-family:&amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;,sans-serif&quot;&gt;The principle of residential development at ground-floor\r\nlevel in this local retail parade is not an acceptable use and would create\r\nharm to the future of the local retail parade which is not in keeping with\r\npolicy 42 and 53 of Waltham Forests LP1 (2024).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: Arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;The failure to account for cycle storage for the proposed three-bedroom flat would fail to promote active travel and there would not be appropriate room to provide cycle storage in the future due to squashed and sized compromised development and therefore the development is unacceptable and contrary to Policy 61 of Waltham Forests LP1 (2024), and policy T5 of the London Plan (2021).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
